Hi Team,

We have successfully completed the Salesforce SAML Passkey POC.

The issue was that although CyberArk was successfully enforcing Passkey authentication, Salesforce was not receiving a recognizable authentication-strength signal and was therefore prompting for a separate Salesforce Passkey.

We resolved this by adding the following SAML attribute to the CyberArk Salesforce application:

AMR = passkey

After retesting, Salesforce successfully recognized the CyberArk Passkey authentication and allowed access without prompting for an additional Salesforce-native Passkey.

This confirms the intended authentication flow is now working successfully.

Thanks,
Ben
